        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Polihale State Park, Kauai, Hawaii, Niihau\n- Topics: Geographic location, public accessibility\n\nFacts:\n- Polihale State Park is a remote wild beach on the western side of the Hawaiian island of Kauai.\n- Polihale State Park is the westernmost publicly accessible area in Hawaii.\n- Niihau is a privately owned island that lies farther west than Polihale State Park.\n- Niihau is the westernmost and seventh largest inhabited island in Hawaii.",
